- expose the graph runtime through `node scripts/zeus.mjs graph ...`;
- let `zeus compile` request bounded graph evidence with repeatable `--graph-seed <seed>` arguments;
- attach fresh/stale graph status, seed resolution, fingerprint, context/impact and verification frontier to compiled JSON;
- append a concise repository-intelligence section to human compile output when graph evidence is requested;
- feed changed-file seeds into `zeus impact`;
- translate graph verification commands into additive ZEUS checks;
- raise impact risk to at least high when graph verification is protected or uncertain;
- stale/missing graph state fails closed to the protected verification frontier instead of being interpreted as safety;
- extend the existing repository-intelligence workflow with syntax and compile/impact integration regressions.

## Invariants

