## Regression coverage

The integration test builds a fresh graph, proves protected `packages/bim-core` evidence reaches compile and impact, then introduces a temporary relevant untracked source file and proves both paths detect stale graph state and fail closed.

## Parent status

This advances #321's compile/impact integration. Keep #321 open after this PR because gate-ledger/evidence recording integration is still a separate remaining acceptance item.

Refs #328.

## Why
The merged adaptive CTO/runtime work covers the main ceilings and control loop, but several explicit #328 invariants were still only described in the issue, not represented or validated in the executable contract. The runtime start receipt also omitted `browserInteractions` even though finish/checkpoint efficiency accounting already enforced it.

## Changes
- expose `browserInteractions` in the runtime start receipt so start/checkpoint/finish share one budget surface;
- require continual-harness `last-used`, archival/expiry review and semantic deduplication lifecycle metadata;
- make cache-quality telemetry explicit: hits, misses, protected/current-evidence bypasses + reasons, invalidations, duplicate query suppression and unnecessary misses;
- record used-vs-ceiling telemetry fields and reviewer/regression findings;
- encode adaptive-repair rules for no-progress retries, repeated-failure strategy change and dependent-only evidence invalidation;
- encode de-escalation rules requiring current deterministic evidence while preserving protected Engineering OS/risk minimums;
- extend adaptive self-tests with mutation coverage for these invariants and browser-budget start/finish consistency.

## Scope
Five existing ZEUS adaptive files only. No product code, core tier ceilings, package manifests/lockfiles, Engineering OS authority, repository-intelligence files or release workflows changed.

## Acceptance
Merge only after the focused adaptive CTO/runtime workflows plus Build, Security, CI and Engineering Gate are green on the exact current head.

This advances #328 but does not close it. The issue's final Done condition still requires representative measured quality-per-work evaluation evidence.

## Why

PR #316 contains useful context-retrieval work, but its blanket reductions of the fast/standard/deep context ceilings and continual-harness budget now conflict with the adaptive CTO policy landed in #329/#334: budgets are ceilings, not targets, and broad reductions should be measurement-led.

This PR salvages the high-value retrieval improvements without changing `.zeus/config.json` or any core ZEUS budget.

## Changes

- query-centred snippets instead of always returning the first 1200 characters;
- cold historical ledgers/changelogs/archive/history paths are excluded from normal retrieval and available with `--include-cold`;
- root-level `history/` and `archive/` paths are classified correctly by normalising with a leading slash;
- deduplicate query terms before scoring/snippet selection;
- bound returned heading metadata to four headings;
- report `usedContextChars` and relevant `coldSourcesExcluded`;
- clamp requested source limits to the existing tier source ceiling;
- add deterministic regression coverage and a path-scoped workflow.

## Deliberately unchanged

- fast/standard/deep source ceilings remain 4/10/24;
- context ceilings remain 8000/28000/80000 characters;
- continual-harness prompt budget remains unchanged;
- no product/runtime, persistence, geometry, Rust, Engineering OS, Language System or release-authority changes.

## Verification

Focused workflow runs syntax validation plus `scripts/zeus-context-retrieval.test.mjs`. Full repository CI remains authoritative.

Supersedes the safe retrieval portion of #316. The blanket budget reductions in #316 should not be merged.

## Scope

Implements the first additive layer of #328 without changing the current Zeus 5.0 core config or kernel.

Adds exactly five files:
- `.zeus/adaptive-cto.json`: tool/research/browser/parallelism ceilings, uncertainty and delivery-stop vocabularies, value-of-information policy, capability routing, learning lifecycle and privacy-safe telemetry contract;
- `scripts/zeus-adaptive-budget.mjs`: validates compatibility with the existing `.zeus/config.json`, merges budget views and decides whether another unit of work should be consumed;
- `scripts/zeus-adaptive-budget.test.mjs`: verifies ceilings-not-targets, low-value stopping, ceiling re-evaluation, protected-proof override, reuse, capability routing, parallelism and actual-vs-budget behavior;
- `.zeus/ADAPTIVE-CTO.md`: integration contract;
- `.github/workflows/zeus-adaptive-cto-v1.yml`: path-scoped execution path for formatting, config validation and the standalone adaptive regression suite.

## Defects found and repaired during validation

1. The two new scripts initially failed the repository Prettier gate. A temporary diagnostic asked the repository's pinned Prettier 3.9.6 for its exact rewrite; only the two claimed scripts were formatted, and the diagnostic was removed.
2. After formatting was green, Zeus's drift guard correctly rejected both scripts as unreachable. The root cause was real: no CLI verb, package script, hook, CI step or Zeus importer executed them. This PR adds one dedicated path-scoped workflow rather than weakening the drift guard or prematurely changing `scripts/zeus.mjs` / package.json.

## Safety boundary

This PR does not edit `.zeus/config.json`, `FAST-KERNEL.md`, Engineering OS, evidence/gate/plan/state ledgers, issue #321 repository-intelligence files, package.json, or product runtime. Existing critical-evidence cache prohibition and one-lane mutation discipline remain intact.

The extension cannot lower a Zeus/Engineering OS gate. Protected proof may exceed ordinary soft ceilings only with an explicit expansion reason.

## Exact-head validation

Head `bd648e023e7ecd03cfd374d70082305f2a128697` is green across:
- `ZEUS adaptive CTO v1` dedicated regression workflow;
- Security;
- Build;
- full CI;
- Engineering Gate.

Within full CI, formatting, lint, typecheck, decision-ID checks, toolchain policy, workspace registries, editor dependency boundaries, `zeus-drift-guard-test.mjs`, `pnpm zeus:drift`, `pnpm zeus:validate`, unit tests, Rust checks and browser capability checks all completed successfully.

## Follow-up

Issue #333 / PR #334 is the separate three-file closed-loop runtime layer stacked on this PR. It imports this adviser rather than forking it.

#328 remains open until the reviewed implementation is integrated into the existing Zeus compile/state lifecycle and representative fast/standard/deep evaluations demonstrate the intended reduction in redundant work.

## Scope

Adds `.zeus/REPOSITORY-INTELLIGENCE.md` for issue #321.

The contract integrates repository graph intelligence into Zeus's existing model instead of duplicating it:
- reuses Zeus workspace fingerprints;
- preserves deterministic/declared/observed/inferred provenance;
- adds Arq-specific semantic-vs-renderer, `.arq` persistence, geometry/units and typed-operation impact domains;
- feeds bounded graph context into `compile`;
- uses pre/post impact only to raise risk/blast radius and verification obligations;
- records graph evidence through the existing evidence/gate ledgers;
- preserves Engineering OS and accepted ADR authority;
- defines isolated worktree overlays and portable lesson boundaries.

## Status

Documentation/specification only. Issue #321 remains open until executable tooling, Zeus integration, deterministic tests, current-head evidence and independent review are complete.
